# CodeIgniter 3 Patterns & API Design

## Controller Structure

```php
class Employees extends CI_Controller {
    public function __construct() {
        parent::__construct();
        require_module_access('employees');
        $this->load->model('Employee_model');
    }

    public function index() {
        $data['employees'] = $this->Employee_model->get_all();
        $this->load->view('employees/index', $data);
    }
}
```

**Rule**: `require_module_access()` in constructor (or at top of each public method). Extend `CI_Controller` or `Coaching_Controller` for coaching modules.

## Forms & POST Flow (PRG)

```php
public function save() {
    $rules = [
        'first_name' => 'required|min_length[2]',
        'email' => 'required|valid_email|is_unique[users.email]'
    ];

    if (!$this->form_validation->run($rules)) {
        $this->session->set_flashdata('error', validation_errors());
        redirect('employees/add');
    }

    $result = $this->Employee_model->insert($this->input->post(null, true));
    if ($result) {
        $this->session->set_flashdata('success', 'Employee added successfully');
        redirect('employees');
    }
    log_message('error', 'Employee insert failed');
    $this->session->set_flashdata('error', 'Failed to add employee');
    redirect('employees/add');
}
```

- On validation fail → flashdata + redirect back
- Never `echo` from controller, never return view after POST
- Use `$this->input->post()` / `$this->input->get()`, never raw superglobals

## API Endpoints (JSON)

```php
public function api_get_employees() {
    if (!$this->input->is_ajax_request()) {
        return $this->output
            ->set_status_header(400)
            ->set_content_type('application/json')
            ->set_output(json_encode(['status' => 'error', 'message' => 'Invalid request']));
    }

    $page = (int) ($this->input->post('page') ?: 1);
    $limit = 25;
    $result = $this->Employee_model->paginate(($page - 1) * $limit, $limit);

    $this->output->set_content_type('application/json');
    return $this->output->set_output(json_encode([
        'status' => 'success',
        'data' => $result['data'],
        'total' => $result['total'],
        'per_page' => $limit,
        'current_page' => $page
    ]));
}
```

HTTP codes: 200/201 success, 400 bad request, 401 unauthorized, 403 forbidden, 404 not found, 422 validation, 500 server error.

## Views

```php
<input type="text" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($employee['email'], ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') ?>">
```

Forms must include CSRF: `form_hidden($this->security->get_csrf_token_name(), $this->security->get_csrf_hash())`

## AJAX

```js
$.ajaxSetup({
    statusCode: { 401: function() { window.location = BASE_URL + 'auth/login'; } }
});

$.ajax({
    url: BASE_URL + 'api/employees',
    type: 'POST',
    data: { page: 1 },
    beforeSend: function() { $('#btn-submit').prop('disabled', true); },
    success: function(response) {
        if (response.status === 'success') { toastr.success(response.message); }
        else { toastr.error(response.message); }
    },
    error: function() { toastr.error('An error occurred'); },
    complete: function() { $('#btn-submit').prop('disabled', false); }
});
```

## Avoid

- `echo` in controller
- Re-render view after POST
- `ob_start()`/`ob_end_clean()` — use `$this->load->view('file', $data, true)` for captured HTML
- Mix JSON + PRG in same endpoint
- Unescaped `<?= $var ?>` in views
